["home/dishwasher-loading-mistakes","The Big One: Blocking The Spray Path","Most dishwasher complaints are loading problems: water cannot clean what the spray arm cannot reach, and the top rack's tallest item is usually the culprit. Facing, spacing and the cutlery basket have right answers, and they are free.","The spray path","Tall items under the arm stop the whole upper rack.","Facing matters","Bowls face the spray; plates face the centre.","Spacing rules","Touching items shield each other from the wash.","The cutlery basket","Mixed orientation beats neat rows for cleaning.","What never goes in","Wood, cast iron and sharp knives stay out.","The detergent dose","More soap leaves film, not cleaner dishes.","Load like you are building for the water jets and the machine's reputation recovers immediately. The fix is free and takes one reload.","home"],
["tech/phone-wont-connect-to-wifi","The Thirty-Second Pair","Wi-Fi connection failures resolve in a fixed ladder: the thirty-second radio toggle, the forget-and-rejoin, then the restarts, with one DHCP setting almost nobody checks at the end. Work the ladder lightest-first and the network comes back.","The thirty-second pair","Airplane mode and Wi-Fi toggle fix more than expected.","Forget and rejoin","Stale saved profiles carry wrong passwords silently.","Restart order","Phone first, then the router; order matters.","The hidden setting","Private MAC and randomised addresses break some routers.","Band steering","2.4 and 5 gigahertz behave as different networks.","When it is the router","One device failing says device; all devices say router.","The ladder exists so no one resets a network that was never broken. Ten minutes, lightest fix first, and the phone rejoins.","tech"],
["entertainment/reviews/fifty","The Axes","Fifty puts four women on screen a week before their fiftieth birthdays and lets the interior do the talking: the Ikoyi penthouse, the marriage bed, the careers that look perfect from outside. The film proved the Nigerian middle-class interior is a cinematic space with its own grammar.","The interior as set","Penthouse and bedroom carry the film's whole argument.","Four performances","An ensemble that shares the frame without competing.","The milestone frame","One birthday week as the film's clock.","Middle-class Nollywood","A market segment the industry had underserved.","The axes","Economics, marriage, friendship and time.","What the film earns","Its quiet scenes land because the loud ones are rare.","Fifty's achievement is scope-within-restraint: a chamber piece that trusts its audience to read a room. The review's job is to say where that trust pays off.","entertainment"],
