["writers/learn/structure-formatting/how-to-use-headings-effectively","Why They Matter","Headings are the reader's map and the writer's outline wearing the same clothes: they promise what follows, scan for the impatient, and force the piece into visible structure. Used well they make long writing feel short.","The promise test","Every heading names what its section delivers.","Scanning first","Most readers scan headings before any sentence.","The outline role","Headings written first keep the draft honest.","Hierarchy honestly","Two levels carry most nonfiction; three carry nearly all.","Parallel shape","Matched heading grammar reads as competence.","The skim reader","If headings tell the story, the piece survives skimming.","Headings are the cheapest editing tool available: write them first, revise them last, and the structure checks itself twice.","writers"],
["writers/learn/writing-process/the-writing-process","Step-By-Step","The writing process is a repeatable ten-stage route from idea to published piece: capture, focus, research, outline, draft, rest, revise, edit, proof and publish. Each stage has a different job, and confusing them is the source of most writerly misery.","Capture first","Ideas are recorded raw and cheap, never judged early.","Research before draft","Facts gathered once beat facts checked twice.","Outline the argument","Structure decided outside the draft saves rewrites.","The ugly draft","Drafting and editing are enemies in the same room.","Rest before revise","Distance is a free editing tool few writers use.","Proof last","Surface errors are fixed in the final pass, only then.","The process matters because it separates jobs that fight each other when mixed. Writers who stage the work finish more and suffer less.","writers"],
["fitness/exercise-for-bone-density-explained","What Bone Responds To","Bone adapts to load the way muscle does, and the loads that count are impact and heavy resistance rather than the smooth motion of swimming and cycling. The age-by-age picture is encouraging: the skeleton responds to training at every adult decade.","Impact counts","Bone answers the forces that push through it.","Heavy resistance","Loads near the top of a safe range are the signal.","Why swimming does not","Weightless environments spare the skeleton the stimulus.","The age-by-age plan","Youth builds the bank; middle age defends it; later years keep it.","The honest caveats","Diagnosed osteoporosis changes the safe exercise menu.","Frequency","Short, frequent loading beats the weekly long session.","The evidence supports a simple hierarchy: lift, jump if you can, walk always. Bone is living accounting, and the deposits are mechanical.","fitness"],
["home/appliances-that-use-the-most-electricity","The Heavy Line-Up","The household electricity ranking is stable across markets: thermal appliances lead, entertainment and computing follow, and the rest is rounding. The ranking exists to aim effort at the levers that actually move the bill.","Heating leads","Thermal loads dominate every honest ranking.","The water heater","Stored hot water is the quiet second place.","Entertainment stack","Consoles and large panels add up at evening peak.","The vampire load","Standby power is small per device and large per household.","The usage meter","Kill-a-watt style meters settle arguments cheaply.","The lever that matters","Hours of use beat wattage in almost every case.","The ranking is a map for effort, not a list of guilt. Change the hours on the top three rows and the bill follows.","home"],
["home/winter-home-preparation","The Freeze Plan On One Card","Winter preparation is a card of priorities: the freeze plan for pipes, the temperature baseline that protects the fabric, the rooms that fail first and the habits that carry the season. It is written to be read before the first cold night, not during it.","The freeze plan","Pipe insulation and drip taps defeat most burst-pipe disasters.","The baseline temperature","Eighteen degrees protects the building as much as the people.","The failing rooms","Loft corners and north walls lose the heat war first.","The boiler service","Annual service is cheaper than the emergency visit.","Gutter discipline","Clear gutters before the first freeze, not after.","The quiet risks","Condensation and mould grow on winter habits.","The one-card plan exists so the seasonal work is a single afternoon rather than a December of small emergencies. Tape it inside the cupboard door and winter becomes ordinary.","home"],
